### R1-CORR-004 (MIN): forward-mode log block uses tab-indent inconsistent with restore-mode

**Bug:** scripts/enable-required-check.sh lines 969-971 emit literal tab characters before `- **Required check:**`, `- **enforce_admins:**`, `- **Plan-only:**`. The restore-mode block at lines 932-935 emits these fields flush-left. Cosmetic inconsistency in the rendered log markdown.

**Fix:** remove the leading tab characters in the forward-mode log block at lines 969-971. Match the flush-left style of the restore-mode block.

### R1-CORR-005 (MIN): prior_restore_evidence_present awk strips both + and - diff line prefixes equally

**Bug:** scripts/enable-required-check.sh prior_restore_evidence_present line 479 awk pattern `sub(/^[+-]/, "", line)`. This strips both `+` (added) AND `-` (removed) diff-line prefixes. An operator REMOVING an old `**Restoring TO:**` entry from the working-tree (uncommitted deletion) would be misidentified as prior-restore evidence → exit 2.

**Fix:** change the regex to strip only `+` (added lines):
```awk
sub(/^[+]/, "", line)
# only added lines are counted as new prior-restore evidence;
# removed lines (^-) are explicitly ignored.
```
OR use a smarter awk that tracks the `+`/`-` prefix separately and only sets `found=1` when the line is an addition. The simpler `^[+]` only is preferred.

Add test: working-tree state with a removed `- **Restoring TO:**` line → assert prior_restore_evidence_present returns FALSE.

