s\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:2883:- **Restoring TO:**\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:2918:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:2930:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3091:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3103:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3118:    '- **Restoring TO:**' \\\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3145:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3157:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3184:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3196:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3223:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3235:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3257:- **Restoring TO:**\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3281:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3304:- **Restoring TO:**\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3328:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3340:  \"required_pull_request_reviews\": {\"dismiss_stale_reviews\": true},\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:858:4. Logs a stderr WARNING about required PAT scope (`administration:write` on the single target repo).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:865:For multi-maintainer adopters who want review enforcement: the script *preserves* any existing `required_pull_request_reviews` shape rather than nulling it (per 020G fix-round-1 SAF-002 closure). Configure your review-shape via the standard GitHub UI or API; the SCP helper won't touch it. **Multi-maintainer adopters MUST also set `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`** — see §12.7.4 for the security rationale and the helper's stderr WARNING when this is missing.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:896:1. **Approving review** from a member listed in your repo's CODEOWNERS for the paths the bypass affects. (This is the adopter's own CODEOWNERS file, not SCP's.) **Minimum-necessary path: `output/findings/waivers.json`** — every bypass PR adds a waiver entry per Gate 3 below, so CODEOWNERS coverage on this path guarantees Gate 1 fires on every bypass PR. Extend coverage to `services.yml`, `policies/**` (if you mirror policies locally), and any other SCP-governed paths in your repo, but do NOT omit `waivers.json` — without it, a bypass PR that touches only the wrapper or only a non-listed path slips through Gate 1.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:904:- **Multi-maintainer adopters.** Configure branch protection with `required_approving_review_count >= 1`, `require_code_owner_reviews: true`, **AND `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`**. (GitHub enforces non-self-approval at the platform level — there is no separate REST API field for that constraint; the WP-SCP-020 plan corpus uses `require_review_from_non_author: true` as shorthand for this platform behaviour, but no API field needs to be set.) Gate 1 is **machine-enforced** — a bypass PR cannot merge without a CODEOWNER review from someone other than the author. The `dismiss_stale_reviews: true` setting is non-optional in this mode: without it, an approving CODEOWNER review on an initial commit persists across subsequent commits in the same PR, so an attacker who obtains a clean review can later push commits that add `.scp/rule-config.yaml disable: true`, change `scp_bypass: true`, or weaken the wrapper's fork-PR `if:` — and merge without re-review. Dismissal fires on ANY push to the PR branch regardless of which files the new commit touches — it is not path-selective. Stale-review dismissal is the enforcement complement to `require_code_owner_reviews`. The `enable-required-check.sh` helper preserves your existing review-shape verbatim and does NOT set `dismiss_stale_reviews: true` for you; configure it explicitly via the GitHub branch-protection UI or API. (As of fix-round-5 of this slice, `enable-required-check.sh` emits a stderr WARNING when the preserved existing review config has `dismiss_stale_reviews: false` — see also the \"verify the gate is live\" block in §12.7.3.)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1239:That SHA is the integrity anchor for Gate 3. Do not substitute `main` HEAD or any other arbitrary commit.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1241:#### Gate 3 - RE-ENABLE\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1251:This slice keeps Gate 3 manual. Automated wrapper-SHA verification is deferred to slice `024B-extras-2`; see `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
